{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Sending batches","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport"],"anchor":"Sending-batches"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transport","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Encoding","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transport","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations13HTTPTransportP","text":"HTTPTransport","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Encoding","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations12BatchEncoderP","text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The wire shape, for a server that ingests these batches:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"One request per batch, in the order the delivery hands them over, the next batch sent only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"once the previous one is delivered or dropped.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The method is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST"},{"type":"text","text":" and the URL is the configured endpoint."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The header fields are the configured ones, then the trace context of the batch’s first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record, then ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content-Type"},{"text":", each replacing fields of the same name before it:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The instrument injects the first (oldest) record’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/context"},{"type":"text","text":", so a server"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"extracting it joins the request, and the events, to the trace the app was in. Its field"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names are the instrument’s: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"traceparent"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracestate"},{"type":"text","text":" for a W3C Trace Context tracer."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record tracked outside any span, or an instrument that injects nothing (the default"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoOpInstrument"},{"type":"text","text":" when none is bootstrapped), adds no fields."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Only the first record’s context travels in the header fields, though a batch may hold","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records tracked in other traces. A server that needs each record’s context reads it from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the body, where a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"text":" writes it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content-Type"},{"type":"text","text":" is always the encoder’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/contentType","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", whatever a configured"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"field or the instrument wrote."}]}]}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is exactly the encoder’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/body","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for the batch’s records, oldest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first. The format is the encoder’s; events need no ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A response with a 2xx status means the batch arrived.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A request the transport can never send (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportError\/invalidRequest(reason:)","type":"reference"},{"text":": a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"malformed or unsupported URL, or an ","type":"text"},{"code":"http","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" URL App Transport Security refuses) isn’t sent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No response, a 5xx status, 408 Request Timeout or 429 Too Many Requests means it didn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"arrive yet: the same request is sent again after the backoff’s next wait, for as long as it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"takes. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Retry-After","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" field is not read; the backoff alone sets the wait.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Any other status means the endpoint won’t take the batch, and it isn’t sent again.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record can arrive twice: a request the server took whose response was lost is sent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again, and a record a store redelivers after the app was stopped mid-send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/isRedelivered"},{"type":"text","text":") may have arrived before. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the one it was"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first sent with, so an encoder that writes each record’s identifier lets the server keep one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"copy."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" returns once the batch is delivered, dropped, or the delivery is cancelled, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a tracker’s store keeps the records of a batch until it arrives, and a batch still being","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"retried when the app ends is delivered again on the next launch. A batch the endpoint rejects,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose request can’t be sent, or that the encoder can’t encode is dropped: logged at error","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"level and reported on ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Each failed attempt that will be retried is logged at notice level.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Cancelling the delivery cancels the send in flight or the wait before the next one, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" returns without logging or reporting it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"While a batch is retried, the delivery’s later batches wait in this destination’s buffer,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which drops its oldest batch when full and reports it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliver(to:batchBufferLimit:bufferDropReporter:)"},{"text":"). With a store, a dropped batch’s records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"aren’t lost: once this destination has caught up, the delivery reads them back from the store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and hands them to it again, in the same run, so they are sent once the endpoint answers.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Without a store, the records of a dropped batch are lost.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let collector = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: collectorURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder())","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: collector)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"HTTPDestination.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination.swift#L67"},"symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","title":"HTTPDestination","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HTTPDe